%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 6f37df8d20f74e62a3e88f7fa41df9b0, type: 3}
  m_Name: Bending Lesson
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  panelTitle: BENDING AND LOAD PATH
  minimumMessageDuration: 3.5
  fadeDuration: 0.2
  slideDistance: 24
  enableSlowMotion: 1
  simulationTimeScale: 0.5
  vehicleEnteredProgress: 0.1
  vehicleMidpointProgress: 0.5
  highStressThreshold: 0.7
  vehicleStuckDelay: 5
  simulationStarted: Simulation started. Watch the vehicle approach the bridge. Bending
    from live load begins only after the wheels transfer weight onto the roadway.
  liveLoadStarted: As the vehicle moves, its weight creates bending in the road.
    The upper side is compressed while the lower side is pulled in tension.
  vehicleEnteredBridge: The live load is now transferring through the road into the
    supporting members and anchors.
  vehicleReachedMidpoint: The vehicle is near midspan, where bending demand is often
    greatest. Deeper triangular support can reduce this bending.
  highStressDetected: Orange or red members are carrying a high percentage of their
    capacity. Their position shows where the load path needs more support.
  stressLimitExceeded: The bridge exceeded the contract's allowed stress. Reduce
    bending demand with a deeper structure or a clearer load path before testing
    again.
  firstMemberBreak: A member exceeded its capacity under bending or axial force.
    Observe how the remaining load redistributes through the bridge.
  vehicleStuck: The live load has stopped moving. Check the road alignment and clearance
    around this area.
  vehicleFailed: The load path was interrupted. Strengthen the failed area or improve
    the bridge geometry before testing again.
  bridgeSucceeded: The bridge carried the live load successfully. Its depth and connected
    members controlled bending throughout the crossing.
  simulationStopped: Simulation stopped. Return to editing when you are ready to
    revise the design.
